# Performance Optimization

## Database Performance

```typescript
// ✅ Add indexes for queried fields
index("user_email_idx").on(t.email),
index("post_created_at_idx").on(t.createdAt),
index("post_user_id_idx").on(t.userId), // FK indexes

// ✅ Use select to limit columns
const posts = await db.select({
  id: posts.id,
  name: posts.name
}).from(posts);

// ✅ Paginate with limits
.limit(10).offset(page * 10)
```

## React Query Optimization

```typescript
// ✅ Set stale times for stable data
api.posts.getLatest.useQuery(undefined, {
  staleTime: 1000 * 60 * 5, // 5 minutes
});

// ✅ Prefetch on server
await api.posts.getLatest.prefetch();

// ✅ Invalidate after mutations
const utils = api.useUtils();
await utils.posts.getLatest.invalidate();
```

## Development Tools

```typescript
// ✅ Conditionally render dev tools
{process.env.NODE_ENV === "development" && (
  <ReactQueryDevtools initialIsOpen={false} />
)}

// ✅ Dev-only timing middleware
if (t._config.isDev) {
  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, waitMs));
}
```

## Server Components

```typescript
// ✅ Use Server Components by default
export default async function Page() {
  // Fetch on server
  await api.posts.prefetch();
  return <ClientComponent />;
}

// ✅ Client Components only when needed
"use client";
export function InteractiveComponent() { }
```

